                <pb facs="0525" n="413" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg413"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24595/3.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Monroe to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                            Jose</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-05-14"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 14, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Monroe says all wounded have been brought to San Jose and that he has
                    disbursed part of Red Cross funds for blankets for them and to aid temporary
                    hospital and that there is sufficient money for present use. States he is
                    informed by Panama authorities of arrival of 250 tents and 500 blankets. Adds
                    that the rainy season has begun, that zinc and lumber for temporary shelter is
                    scarce, but that local permanent charitable organization has affairs well
                    regulated.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
